course: dictionary
lesson: 2981
title: A land ruled by a duke
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A duchy is an area of land ruled by a duke or a duchess. The word has the same start as duke and duchess, so you can guess it is about their land.
explain: Read the context: «The Grand Duchy of Lithuania took most Ukrainian lands in the 14th century; its rulers were Lithuanian.» The word Grand and the mention of rulers tell you a duchy is a land with a ruler, and that the ruler is in charge of the whole place.
explain: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence. Try «The land ruled by a duke took most Ukrainian lands in the 14th century.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Duchy means an area of land ruled by a duke or a duchess.
fact: «Duchy» is a noun, and its plural is duchies.
fact: The Duchy of Cornwall and the Duchy of Lancaster are special estates of land owned by the British royal family.
fact: Normandy was once a duchy, and history lessons often mention duchies in medieval Europe.
fact: Related words are duke, duchess, kingdom and principality.
exercise: «The Grand Duchy of Lithuania took most Ukrainian lands in the 14th century.» What is a duchy? | A large building for storing grain | A kind of fast boat | A school subject about numbers | *An area of land ruled by a duke or duchess
exercise: The Duchy of Cornwall is a special estate. Who owns it? | The Scottish parliament | A family of local farmers | *The British royal family | A football club
exercise: Which word is a ruler of a duchy? | forest | bridge | sandwich | *duke
test: Which word means a land ruled by a king or queen? | duchy | estate | duchess | *kingdom
test: In history, «The Duchy of Normandy» tells the reader what about Normandy? | *It was a land ruled by a duke | It was a sea full of ships | It was a famous kind of cheese | It was a type of castle wall
exam: Which sentence uses duchy correctly? | *The Duchy of Lancaster is land owned by the British royal family. | The duchy was a hot drink served at breakfast. | Duchy is the loud noise a door makes. | I ran to the duchy to catch the bus.
